        "‘Him who knew no sin he made to be sin’ (2 Corinthians 5:21) is striking. Some scholars note that in the Greek Old Testament <em>hamartia</em> can mean ‘sin offering’ (as in Leviticus 4), and read it that way here. Others read it as Christ fully identifying with sinful humanity. Both readings say the sinless one entered our place."
