        "Romans 5:8 says the same: ‘God commends his own love toward us, in that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.’ The cross is God’s love on display, not a price that changed God’s mind. And Jesus speaks of laying down his life of his own accord (John 10:18), in perfect union with the Father (John 10:30).",
        "Even the cry of dereliction, ‘My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?’ (Mark 15:34), quotes Psalm 22, a psalm that ends in praise because God ‘has not hidden his face from him; but when he cried to him, he heard’ (Psalm 22:24)."
