        "Ephesians 1:10 says God’s plan is ‘to sum up all things in Christ’. The verb is <em>anakephalaioō</em>, which contains the word <em>kephalē</em>, ‘head’. HELPS describes it as showing ‘the head as the ‘organizing center,’ causing all the parts to work together in harmony’.",
        "The only other New Testament use is Romans 13:9, where all the commandments are ‘summed up’ in ‘love your neighbour’. Christ does for all things what love does for the law: he gathers them, gives them their meaning and holds them together.",
