        "J. B. Torrance and T. F. Torrance spoke of Christ’s ‘vicarious humanity’. Not only did Christ die in our place; he lived in our place. He believed, obeyed, prayed and worshipped as one of us and for us. Hebrews calls him the ‘author and perfecter of faith’ (Hebrews 12:2). Our faith rests on his faithfulness.",
        "Baxter Kruger’s <em>Jesus and the Undoing of Adam</em> brings this to ordinary readers: in Jesus, Adam’s fearful, hiding way of being was brought to an end, and a new way of being human, as a beloved son, began."
