        "Relational and universalist writers (Thomas Talbott among them) reply that Paul’s argument depends on the parallel: if ‘all’ means everyone in the first half of 5:18, it is natural to read ‘all’ the same way in the second half. And ‘receive’ in 5:17 can describe receiving a gift given, not a condition for its being given.",
        "This is genuinely debated. A middle position, common in this stream, is that Christ has really included all humanity in his undoing of Adam, and that each person is invited to receive and live in that new humanity."
