        "Athanasius summed up the purpose of the incarnation in these terms: ‘He was made man that we might be made God’. Irenaeus said the Son ‘became what we are, that He might bring us to be even what He is Himself’. In both cases the idea is sharing by grace in what the Son has by nature.",
